\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 My Approach\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\b0\fs24 \cf2 (Combined philosophy + what happens during a visit)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i0 \cf2 A piano is a complex, interconnected system. There are a thousand small adjustments that can make a piano sing. All the parts affect and influence each other.\
I see each visit as an opportunity to improve your instrument as a whole \'97 tuning, touch, and tone \'97 with attention to both musical detail and mechanical integrity. I also love to interact with the humans who play it\'97both large and small\'97and I\'92m always eager to learn and share my knowledge and excitement!\
When I arrive at your piano, I\'92ll remove the outer case and do a quick evaluation, noting any repairs needed and what improvements can be made. Then I\'92ll do a light clean and vaccuum, and make sure your bench legs are nice and tight. Then I\'92ll tune, and with any time left over, I\'92ll work on making any improvements I can to touch and tone.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 About\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf2 I\'92ve always been drawn to the intersection of sound, structure, and craft. I\'92ve played piano since I was five years old. I started out university as a jazz piano major, and ended up with a degree in mathematics!\
A piano is both mechanical system and expressive instrument \'97 steel, wood, felt, tension, and vibration working together to produce something deeply human. What I love about this work is that it requires both analytical precision and sensitive listening.\
Tuning is only part of the picture. The feel of the keys, the consistency of the action, the balance of tone across the keyboard \'97 these elements shape how an instrument responds to the player.\
I tune primarily by ear, guided by a deep understanding of harmonic structure and acoustics. I also make intelligent use of modern tools when they enhance precision and efficiency. I think of the approach as high-tech analog \'97 grounded in craft, informed by science.\
Just as important to me is the human side of the work. I value clear communication, respect for your home, and sharing knowledge about the instrument. I enjoy demystifying what\'92s happening inside the piano and helping you feel more connected to it.\
At its best, this work is quiet, attentive, and deeply satisfying.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

