\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 Frequently Asked Questions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl288\slmult1\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
How often should a piano be tuned?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Most pianos benefit from tuning once or twice per year. Instruments that are played frequently, used for lessons, or that experience greater than normal seasonal humidity changes may benefit from tuning twice a year or more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl288\slmult1\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
My piano hasn\'92t been tuned in years. Is that okay?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Yes! Your piano might need a \'93pitch correction\'94 or \'93pitch raise\'94 to bring it back to standard pitch and restore its intended voice. I include this service at no extra charge, though it does take up some of the time I generally reserve for other improvements.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl288\slmult1\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
Will my piano need tuning if it hasn't been played much?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 It\'92s not the playing of the piano itself that causes it to go out of tune, but rather changes in temperature and humidity, as well as the settling of the piano itself. The amount of use a piano receives rarely has a significant impact on its tuning, unless a pianist plays exceptionally hard.\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

